R2.

Problem : Thread Safe in memory file system qith wildcard search.
Implement File system with :

mkdir(path) - create dirs recursively
addFile(filePath, content) - create/append file, auto create parent dirs
readFile(filePath) - return content
ls(path) - if file -> [fileName] : if dir -> sorted immediate childern
search(pattern) - return matching file path supports _ (any sequence) ? (single)
find("/a/b/_.txt") - ["a/b/c.txt", "a/b/d.txt"]
find("/a/b/?.txt") - ["a/b/c.txt", "a/b/d.txt"]
Assume there will only one special/regex char and that too in the last part

Requirements : thread safe (optimized for reads), efficienmt search (avoid full scan)


